messages:
maria_support: FYI Acme reported JSON mode streaming output truncated mid-object — client sees: '{\n  \"id\": \"abc123\",\n  \"items\": [1,2,3' and parser throws EOF. They say it happens ~10% of streams, mostly behind their F5 LB.

olga_repro: Can you paste the full HTTP stream (raw) or a curl command we can run to repro? Also what SDK/version and whether they're using SSE vs chunked responses.

maria_support: Customer sent this curl (trimmed):
```
curl -i -N -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \\n  -H "Accept: text/event-stream" \\n  https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate?stream=true&mode=json
```
They get a sequence of SSE events, then the socket closes without final event or trailing braces.

vikram_eng: This smells like an LB idle-timeout / upstream-close. If the origin closes mid-chunk the SSE client will see partial JSON. Can we get nginx/ELB logs from the customer's side or our edge?

leo_sre: Pulled edge proxy logs for that customer window — see upstream prematurely closed connection entries:
```
2026/11/02 16:11:23 [error] 12345#0: *98765 upstream prematurely closed connection while reading response header from upstream, client: 10.0.0.5, server: api.redwood.ai, request: \"GET /v1/generate?stream=true&mode=json HTTP/1.1\", upstream: \"http://10.21.34.56:8080/\", host: \"api.redwood.ai\"
```
Also see LB logs with TCP FIN ~9s after last payload chunk.

vikram_eng: Ok that matches. Two actionable items: (1) client-side: be resilient to truncated JSON in streaming mode — parse incrementally and treat unexpected EOF as retriable partial response OR buffer until valid JSON found. (2) server-side: emit periodic keepalive SSE comments or a one-byte comment every N seconds to keep LB idle timers from triggering. Also ensure final sentinel event (e.g., `data: [DONE]`) is flushed before closing.

olga_repro: I created a small repro script that simulates an upstream closing mid-stream (node):
```js
// repro-server.js (node)
const http = require('http');
http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream', 'Cache-Control': 'no-cache' });
  res.write('data: {"id":"x","items":[');
  setTimeout(() => {
    res.write('1,2');
    // abruptly end connection to simulate LB drop
    res.socket.destroy();
  }, 2000);
}).listen(8081);
```
Run a client that expects valid JSON -> it fails. Repro is reliable when I forcibly close the socket.

maria_support: Customer asks if they'll be billed for partial streams — they reported payment for a request that never completed.

sam_billing: For hosted API billing is per-token produced/returned. If we cut off mid-stream tokens already returned are billable. We can offer a one-off credit if the customer proves the stream was unusable and it impacted production; I'll coordinate offline.

leo_sre: Longer-term server fixes: (a) configure our front LB to increase idle timeout for streaming routes to 120s (default was 60s for this region), (b) ensure our runtime emits a newline/comment keepalive every 15s when no tokens are produced, (c) guarantee final flush + `data: [DONE]\n\n`. I've opened an internal infra change ticket.

vikram_eng: Also note proxies that buffer responses (some CDNs) may require `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` and `X-Accel-Buffering: no` (for nginx). Suggest adding these headers for streaming endpoints.

maria_support: Customer is using Dedicated behind their own F5 — they said they can't change LB timeout quickly. Any immediate mitigations?

vikram_eng: For Dedicated customers we can enable server-side periodic keepalive (no infra change) by toggling runtime flag `stream.keepalive_interval=15s` per-customer. That should avoid timeouts without touching their LB. Can ops toggle for Acme?

leo_sre: I can enable it for their cluster; will need a maintenance window to flip and monitor. Scheduling in next 2 hours.

olga_repro: Added a gist with minimal client-side parser suggestion: attempt to JSON.parse only complete top-level objects; if parsing fails due to EOF, retry the request with the same prompt + `resume_from_token` param we discussed. Example pseudo-code in gist.

maria_support: Great. Customer also wants a short guidance doc we can send (why this happens + quick fixes). Can someone draft a 3-bullet note?

vikram_eng: Draft: (1) Keepalives: our streaming endpoints send periodic SSE comments to keep connections alive; if you run your own LB ensure idle timeouts > 60s. (2) Client resilience: implement incremental parsing + retry on EOF with idempotency key. (3) If using Dedicated, request `stream.keepalive_interval=15s` from support to avoid midstream LB closures.

maria_support: Thanks. Please track action items.

incidentbot: Created ticket INC-3421: "Streaming JSON truncated by LB idle close — AcmeCorp — enable keepalive and adjust timeouts" assigned to leo_sre, vikram_eng.

vikram_eng: I'll follow up with a small runtime patch to add an explicit final sentinel chunk and a shorter keepalive default for streaming-mode. Will post PR once ready.

maria_support: Marking this thread for escalation resolution once infra change is verified with Acme. :thumbsup:
